# Formats staged files with Prettier before the commit is written.
#
# This exists because CI's `pnpm format:check` gates the `deploy-web` job (it
# runs inside `verify`, and `deploy-web` has `needs: verify`) — so a single
# unformatted file does not just fail a check, it silently skips the
# production deploy. That happened for four consecutive pushes to main, and
# nobody noticed for ~15 hours, because a skipped job reads as an absence
# rather than a failure.
#
# Only staged files are touched, so this stays fast enough to not be worth
# bypassing. If you ever genuinely need to, `git commit --no-verify` skips it.
pnpm lint-staged
